Davidababcock@student.cascadia.edu wrote:

> Poison resistance is helpful and can avoid some painful YASDs,
> wouldn't be a bad idea, but remember, there are plenty of other
> nonpoisonous creatures that grant that intrinsic.

Suggests blessed tinning kit which I just discussed in another posting. 
I should have put that paragraph here.

> Save at least one wish for after you go through sokoban: wish for a
> BoH if you don't get one. I highly suggest going for a magic marker;
> you'll find plenty of junk scrolls later on which you can blank, and
> if your luck is high, you'll be able to write any spellbook you want
> with a very low rate of failure (Ask for it blessed if you don't care
> about losing the ability to make reverse-genocide and level-teleport
> scrolls; you'll save some holy water that way)

The later in the game the more valuable the magic marker in my opinion. 
Early on I want other basics.

> You're elven, so wishing for the SoA would be a bad idea, and
> magicbane is very easy to acquire for wizards... Perhaps a spellbook
> you really want and cannot write yet? Or maybe a +3 Helm of Brilliance/
> Wizard's hat (forgot the name, the one that looks like dunce cap but
> isn't) or +3 gauntlets of dexterity.

This early in the game I think the SDSM gives enough armor that the rest
is fluff until later.  Go for the mines end luckstone, the Sokoban
prize.  Use the mine town altar to get Magicbane (first wizard gift) and
maybe Stormbringer (crowning gift and so on occasion crowning is a good
idea).  For a wizard I like to wield Magicbane almost all of the time
with Stormbringer or another very powerful artifact as my alternate
wield as a backup to get out of a crowd, plus build up a stack of very
good daggers in my quiver.  I'll drop my initial quarterstaff as soon as
I have an artifact and try not to #enhance it unless it's a matter of
life and death.

Then step back and think.  Go for blessed "oR or blessed (oHolding
whichever was not the Sokoban prize.  Or maybe tinning kit for the safer
instrinsics.  Then start thinking about more armor.  Gloves first and
for a wizard dexterity beat the other types.  Boots next probably speed.
Helm of brilliance after that then shirt.

That list is a lot longer than the number of wishes and I'm not positive
which I'd want first, but I would go through the mines and Sokoban and
do some altar camping before using up another wish.


